; Whole places drawn in the editor (drawnplaces.py, the editor's round C). The format: pieces/README.txt.

PLACE:  Saint Odo's Rest
SIZE:   60x34
SIGN:   ± #e8e0c8
LOOK:   A chapel in ruins, its graveyard gone to grass, and a bell tower that still stands. Under it lies a crypt.
WORLD:  land=any road=near level=2 how=one found=map,rumour,book
RUMOUR: They say the monks of Saint Odo's Rest went down into their crypt one winter and none came up. A seal of violet stone shuts the deepest door, broken in three.
BOOK:   "Saint Odo sealed the deep door with a disc of violet stone and broke it in three: one he kept by the altar, one in the bell tower, one with the dead."
LAND:   fitted
THING:  S = seal shard on a plinth do:shard

FLOOR:  ground
MOOD:   A chapel in ruins. Grass grows between the flagstones, and a bell tower stands over the east end.
THING:  P = pressure plate do:pressure
THING:  Q = bars
EVENT:  when=press at=P then=open:Q then=msg:"Something heavy lands on the plate by the altar. In the east wall, bars sink away."
PERSON: Brother Anselm at 25,15 says="The brothers went down to pray for the dead, and stayed with them. Three shards, they say. I will not go down."
